Some more conducts that the game might take note of:

You never were magic-protected.

You could never see.

You never used any means of levitation.

You never caused conflict.

You never wrote "Elbereth".

The last two are of course hardly noteworthy but nor is "You never 
wished for an artifact."

For some of these one might provide help at the game beginning.  For 
example you could be asked if you wish to keep the blindness conduct. 
Then your character would be created with a cursed blindfold on.  Some 
spellbooks might have Braille inscriptions on them (with a certain 
probability), which you could learn by trying to read them often enough. 
The Book of the Dead would always have Braille letters, so you would not 
need to take the blindfold off (and doing so would break the conduct).

If you decide at the beginning not to levitate, means of levitation 
would not be generated randomly.  Similarly for conflict (a bit 
problematic for cavemen).

The first of these conducts, taken together with polyless and 
genocideless would be *very* difficult.  Is there anyone who has ever 
ascended without magic resistance?

